{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:51c2251ff30ca1f5","name":"Rocket Arm","source":{"id":"source:reference-51c2251ff30ca1f5","title":"Rocket Arm","revision":21099,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T01:09:40Z","sha256":"26a0c1e43a767a617b8d8c2c979b46d06ed020533c868fbc2a6bd8cc60b76b40","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21099","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Rocket%20Arm&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-51c2251ff30ca1f5","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scavenger's Guide to Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scavenger%27s_Guide_to_Droids"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Cost:"]}," Appendage Cost x 4\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Weight:"]}," (2 x ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cost Factor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cost_Factor"},") Kilograms\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Availability:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Illegal"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Illegal"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["This ",{"tag":"a","children":["Illegal"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Illegal"}," modification is derived from the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Projectile Appendage"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Projectile_Appendage","referenceId":"reference:e5c1bee958e39c21"}," system available for noncombat ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"},". A Rocket Arm is essentially a hollowed-out ",{"tag":"a","children":["Appendage"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Appendage"}," in which the servo control has been replaced by a short-range rocket engine and fuel. The arm's fine control is eliminated, but the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"}," can point its arm at a target and fire. The arm detaches and flies at the target, detonating the remaining fuel on impact. Rocket Arms are unguided projectiles without targeting computers.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["This ",{"tag":"a","children":["Illegal"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Illegal"}," modification costs 2,000 credits and installation requires a DC 20 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check. Failure on the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check means the rocket might not detach properly when fired, exploding and dealing its damage to the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"}," and all targets in a 1-Square ",{"tag":"a","children":["Splash"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Splash"}," radius. The Rocket Arm is considered to be a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Weapon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Weapon"}," that deals 3d8 points of damage upon detonation, with a 1-square ",{"tag":"a","children":["Splash"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Splash"},".\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
